# Git and GitHub Pages

When you finish meaningful edits in this repo (anything a user would expect to see on the live site or in version control):

1. Run `npm run build` if you changed source and want to verify the build (optional but preferred before deploy).
2. `git add -A`, commit with a clear message, and `git push origin main`.
3. Run `npm run deploy` so the `gh-pages` branch is updated from `dist` (GitHub Pages source for this project).

If there is nothing to commit, still run `git push origin main` and `npm run deploy` when the user explicitly asks to publish.

Use PowerShell-safe paths; the project directory may contain `&` in the path—use explicit `node ./node_modules/...` scripts from `package.json` rather than relying on `.bin` shims if scripts fail.
